From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:20:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: power the internal DCP down for any
 deep sleep

A deep sleep needs the display coprocessor and its domains off: its
display DARTs refuse the sleep while they're on. So a plain suspend with
appledrm.power_gate_ms at its default of 0 was always refused. Power them
down for a deep sleep whatever the parameter says, and leave it deciding
only the power-down after a blank and the one before suspend-to-idle.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 768e7eb92395c4246554b92167e366e2d3528507)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c      |  5 +++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 14 +++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 4a054f1254..6abc6989a3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -8627,8 +8627,9 @@ static int dcp_platform_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	/*
 	 * T8132: setPowerState powers the display down; the coprocessor keeps
 	 * running and its power domains stay on, as below, unless the internal
-	 * display is blanked with appledrm.power_gate_ms set: then the
-	 * coprocessor and its domains are powered down too (iomfb_m4_suspend()).
+	 * display is blanked and this is a deep sleep, or appledrm.power_gate_ms
+	 * is set: then the coprocessor and its domains are powered down too
+	 * (iomfb_m4_suspend()).
 	 */
 	if (iomfb_is_m4(dcp)) {
 		int ret = iomfb_m4_suspend(dcp);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index c987d2afcc..8d5b80001d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 #include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/spinlock.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/soc/apple/dart.h>
 #include <linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h>
 #include <linux/soc/apple/pmp-display.h>
@@ -7864,13 +7865,16 @@ int iomfb_m4_suspend(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 	} else if (dcp->display_off) {
 		/*
 		 * Already powered down by the blank; the next frame powers it up.
-		 * Power the DCP and its domains down too, if it may. That is an
-		 * extra saving, not a condition of sleep: a power-down that cannot
-		 * start leaves the display logically off, and one that fails has
-		 * failed the session already; neither refuses the sleep.
+		 * Power the DCP and its domains down too, if it may: a deep sleep
+		 * needs that whatever power_gate_ms says, or its display DARTs
+		 * refuse it, and elsewhere it is an extra saving. It is not a
+		 * condition of this step: a power-down that cannot start leaves the
+		 * display logically off, and one that fails has failed the session
+		 * already; neither refuses the sleep here.
 		 */
 		ret = 0;
-		if (dcp->gate_capable && READ_ONCE(power_gate_ms) && !dcp->gated)
+		if (dcp->gate_capable && !dcp->gated &&
+		    (READ_ONCE(power_gate_ms) || pm_suspend_via_firmware()))
 			iomfb_m4_power_gate(dcp);
 	} else {
 		ret = dcp_m4_set_power_state(dcp, false);
-- 
2.43.0

